# Overview

## Domain
- Farm-themed multi-agent workspace manager (inspired by Gas Town)
- Agents (LLM-backed CLI tools) are assigned farm roles and collaborate on work orders
- A work order decomposes into tasks; agents produce draft artifacts that merge into canonical output

## Key Concepts
- **Work Order** — top-level goal; contains tasks, artifacts, decisions, events
- **Task** — unit of work; has status lifecycle (NEW→ASSIGNED→IN_PROGRESS→DONE, etc.)
- **Artifact** — content produced by agents; drafts merge into a single canonical artifact
- **Decision** — recorded rationale tied to a work order and optional task
- **Role** — one of 8 farm roles (Farm Manager, Field Hand, Field Scout, Grain Elevator, Bell Ringer, Barn Dog, Heel, Barn Crew) with policy-enforced permissions
- **Agent Session** — a spawned CLI agent (Cursor, Claude, Codex, etc.) bound to a role + task
- **Memory** — embedding-backed knowledge store with semantic recall + time-decay scoring

## User Types
- **Operator** — uses the Desktop console (Electron) to create work orders, assign tasks, spawn agents
- **Observer** — views the read-only Next.js web dashboard for live event streams and status

## Primary Workflows
1. Operator creates a work order → engine emits `workorder.created`
2. Farm Manager assigns tasks to roles → agents are spawned into git worktrees
3. Field Hands work tasks and submit draft artifacts
4. Grain Elevator merges drafts into canonical output (text or JSON merge)
5. Engine tick runs cadence: Bell Ringer ticks, Scout triages, Dogs maintain, Heel alerts
6. All events stream via WebSocket to desktop + web dashboards
